<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds ended up, not far from the record high the market showed on Wednesday, after a weaker mark gave support to peripheral markets.</p>
<p>One dealer said people were buying in anticipation of the budget and a new rate cut by the Bank of Spain. After today's rate cut by Bank of France, the bonos recovered from their initial losses.</p>
<p>The 10-year spread over German bonds dipped to 206 from 216 at yesterday's close, and dealers said they expected it to break below 200 soon.</p>
</text>
